{"title":"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Leah went for a walk and recorded the number of robins, cardinals and blue jays that she saw in the bar graph shown.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Unfortunately, she forgot to include numbers on the vertical axis. If a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> robins, cardinals and blue jays were observed, how many robins did she see?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/1/fb1b8a9118889222de88d5573cf0608b75094dd9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ (A) }\\ 9 \\qquad\\text{ (B) }\\ 12 \\qquad\\text{ (C) }\\ 15 \\qquad\\text{ (D) }\\ 18 \\qquad\\text{ (E) }\\ 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The bars went <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/1/171ca7bd93ed07719d1ed80869652c515af1bddb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 + 3 + 1 = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"116\" height=\"15\" /> ticks up in total, so each tick mark was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/9/ae915aec584fe3ddbff22e01b26ed06e7a64f8d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{30}{10} = 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"57\" height=\"38\" /> up. Since the robins bar was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> ticks up, she must have saw <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35b126d48558d4ef452a14a659ee4828704f605a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 6 = \\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"132\" height=\"30\" /> robins.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28answer_choices.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(answer_choices)\">Solution 2 (answer choices)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (answer choices)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that the number of robins she saw must be more than half of the total (which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />) because the other two bars clearly sum up to less than the number of robins. This means the answer must be D or E.\n</p><p>Next, there were half as many cardinals as robins, so she must have saw an even number of robins. Thus, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/abad8dfada01de80d90752b8b8b54e654fa9981a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf {(D) } 18}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat\">2026 CEMC Fermat</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cemc.math.uwaterloo.ca/contests/past_contests.html\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2026_CEMC_Fermat_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2026 CEMC Fermat Problems/Problem 5\">5